  m_Name: Object_262
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  partName: Exhaust Valve
  description: The Exhaust Valve is a tiny, elongated component located at the top-center-center
    of the engine, made of Material.001, responsible for controlling the flow of
    exhaust gases out of the combustion chamber. Its precise operation is critical,
    as it enables the engine to expel the exhaust gases efficiently, and a notable
    aspect is that it is designed to withstand the high temperatures and pressures
    associated with exhaust gas flow. The exhaust valve's tiny size and elongated
    shape allow it to fit within the engine's compact cylinder head, and its material
    properties enable it to operate effectively in the harsh environment of the exhaust
    system.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
